# 001-switchpt-unflag: drop stale `AI:RemoveDeck:All` from three SwitchPT cards (card-script proposal, NOT applied)
# Cards: Aquamoeba, Turtleshell Changeling, Myr Quadropod. Each is a single `A:AB$ Pump ... AILogic$ SwitchPT` ability;
# PumpAi.java:54-60 already handles that logic (blocks only a second activation per turn).
# Test (AiLabSim, equal life 40/40, 4 games each, 150 s cap): Commander deck Lab001 Alandra (mono-blue) vs Thopter Workshop,
# both shrunk to commander + 29 cards (shrink_deck.py) so the flagged cards get drawn.
#   baseline (flag present): casts 0, activations 0 (Turtleshell sat in hand uncast; Aquamoeba only discarded)
#   patched (flag removed):  casts 7 (Turtleshell 4/4 games, Aquamoeba 2, Myr Quadropod 1), activations 26;
#                            wins A=2 B=2 vs baseline A=1 B=3 (4 games: noise only)
# Re-run at 20/20 life: baseline 0 casts; patched 7 casts, 30 activations (same result).
# CAVEAT (main-session analysis): PumpAi SwitchPT only checks "in combat" and "not already used this turn" (PumpAi:57,:83), so activations are mostly waste. Pair this flag removal with the 0b PumpAi guard (patch 005, planned) before proposing.
# Caveat: Turtleshell activated up to 12 times in one game; the AI uses the switch freely, not always usefully.
# Apply from the repo root with: git apply tools/concordia/ai_lab/patches/001-switchpt-unflag.patch
diff --git a/forge-gui/res/cardsfolder/t/turtleshell_changeling.txt b/forge-gui/res/cardsfolder/t/turtleshell_changeling.txt
index 36e0838c..2f0b06b8 100644
--- a/forge-gui/res/cardsfolder/t/turtleshell_changeling.txt
+++ b/forge-gui/res/cardsfolder/t/turtleshell_changeling.txt
@@ -4,5 +4,4 @@ Types:Creature Shapeshifter
 PT:1/4
 K:Changeling
 A:AB$ Pump | Cost$ 1 U | Defined$ Self | AILogic$ SwitchPT | KW$ HIDDEN CARDNAME's power and toughness are switched | SpellDescription$ Switch CARDNAME's power and toughness until end of turn.
-AI:RemoveDeck:All
 Oracle:Changeling (This card is every creature type.)\n{1}{U}: Switch Turtleshell Changeling's power and toughness until end of turn.
